# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows editor rewriting a file's endings shows up
# as a whole-repo diff of pure CRLF churn with zero content change — 85 files,
# 18k lines, on 2026-08-03 — which buries real changes and turns every touched
# file into a merge-conflict magnet.
#
# eol=lf rather than the usual `text=auto` alone (which would check out CRLF on
# Windows) because this repo's 7 shell scripts run inside Linux containers:
# backend/*/docker-entrypoint.sh and scripts/*.sh would fail with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" if checked out with CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are the one exception — none exist today, so these are
# guards for whenever one is added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
